1. Zemberek dictionaries (zemberek-nlp)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Source:     https://github.com/ahmetaa/zemberek-nlp, morphology/src/main/resources/tr (the default
            dictionaries of TurkishDictionaryLoader), as copied unmodified into Zeyrek 0.1.3.
            Vendored in scripts/lexicon/zemberek/ (see NOTICE.md there for checksums).
Copyright:  Ahmet A. Akın and the zemberek-nlp contributors.
Licence:    Apache License 2.0 (full text at the end of this file).

Shipped as: crates/akana-core/src/morphology/zemberek_lexicon.txt, compiled into the library.
            scripts/build_full_lexicon.py builds it from the Zemberek dictionaries.
Changes:    duplicate entries merged; corpus-collected proper nouns that are inflected common
            words or common words without their Turkish letters, and roots with stray
            characters, dropped; Zemberek's Ref: pointers made lemmas; entries added, replaced,
            respelled and removed by akana's own supplements (scripts/lexicon/akana-legal.dict,
            akana-extra.dict, akana-variants.dict, akana-spelling.dict, akana-remove.dict,
            which carry akana's own attributes Lexicalized, NotLexicalized, Rare and
            Nonstandard); homographs numbered; written in akana's one-line format.

Shipped as: crates/akana-core/src/pii/person_names.txt, compiled into the library: the given
            names of Zemberek's person-names.dict (morphology/src/main/resources/tr), which PII
            masking reads as first names.
Changes:    lower-cased with Turkish rules; forms without circumflexes added.

The morphotactics (crates/akana-core/src/morphology/turkish_morphotactics.rs, stems.rs,
analyzer.rs) port the design of zemberek-nlp's TurkishMorphotactics, StemTransitionsBase and
RuleBasedAnalyzer (Apache License 2.0) to Rust.

crates/akana-core/tests/data/morphology/review/zemberek_tests.tsv is test data, not compiled
into the library. It is part of the source repository and of the crate's source package. It
holds the analysis checks of zemberek-nlp's morphology tests
(morphology/src/test/java/zemberek/morphology/analysis, Apache License 2.0). They were
converted to one check per line, and their dictionary lines were rewritten in akana's
lexicon format.

