2. Universal Dependencies Turkish treebanks BOUN, Kenet, Penn, Tourism, Atis and FrameNet
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Source:     https://github.com/UniversalDependencies/UD_Turkish-BOUN, UD_Turkish-Kenet,
            UD_Turkish-Penn, UD_Turkish-Tourism, UD_Turkish-Atis and UD_Turkish-FrameNet,
            release r2.18: the train and dev splits (no test split).
Authors:    BOUN: Büşra Marşan, Furkan Akkurt, Utku Türk, Furkan Atmaca, Şaziye Betül Özateş,
            Gözde Berk, Seyyit Talha Bedir, Abdullatif Köksal, Balkız Öztürk Başaran, Tunga
            Güngör, Arzucan Özgür (Türk et al. 2022, "Resources for Turkish Dependency Parsing:
            Introducing the BOUN Treebank and the BoAT Annotation Tool", Language Resources and
            Evaluation 56(1), doi:10.1007/s10579-021-09558-0; Marşan et al. 2022,
            arXiv:2207.11782). Kenet: Aslı Kuzgun, Neslihan Cesur, Olcay Taner Yıldız, Oğuzhan
            Kuyrukçu, Arife Betül Yenice, Bilge Nas Arıcan, Ezgi Sanıyar. Penn: Neslihan Cesur,
            Aslı Kuzgun, Olcay Taner Yıldız, Büşra Marşan, Neslihan Kara, Bilge Nas Arıcan, Merve
            Özçelik, Deniz Baran Aslan. Tourism: Aslı Kuzgun, Neslihan Cesur, Olcay Taner Yıldız,
            Oğuzhan Kuyrukçu, Büşra Marşan, Bilge Nas Arıcan, Neslihan Kara, Deniz Baran Aslan,
            Ezgi Sanıyar, Cengiz Asmazoğlu. Atis: Mehmet Köse, Olcay Taner Yıldız. FrameNet:
            Neslihan Cesur, Aslı Kuzgun, Olcay Taner Yıldız, Büşra Marşan, Oğuzhan Kuyrukçu,
            Bilge Nas Arıcan, Ezgi Sanıyar, Neslihan Kara, Merve Özçelik (Marşan et al. 2021,
            "Building the Turkish FrameNet", Proceedings of the 11th Global Wordnet Conference,
            118-125).
Licence:    Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International,
            https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/legalcode

Shipped as: crates/akana-core/src/embeddings/function_lemmas.tsv, compiled into the library.
            DERIVED FROM CC BY-SA DATA: it is distributed under CC BY-SA 4.0.
Changes:    no text is shipped. The table holds, for 20 lemmas, the number of 256-token chunks
            of the BOUN and Kenet sentences (and of a court-decision sample) each occurs in, and
            the weight akana gives it (examples/sparse_idf.rs).

Shipped as: crates/akana-core/src/morphology/prior.tsv.gz, compiled into the library.
            DERIVED FROM CC BY-SA DATA: it is distributed under CC BY-SA 4.0.
Changes:    no text is shipped. The analyzer's frequency prior is estimated
            (examples/morph_prior.rs) from a court-decision word list mixed with the word
            counts of the six treebanks' sentences, with the words the analyzer reads in more
            than one part of speech split among them as the treebanks tag them, and per-word
            corrections that keep those shares. Both inputs are part of the source repository
            and also DERIVED FROM CC BY-SA DATA: data/morphology/prior_general_types.tsv.gz
            (scripts/prior_general_types.py: each word of the sentences and how often it
            occurs) and data/morphology/pos_twins.tsv (scripts/pos_twins.py: for each word form
            read in more than one part of speech, how many times its tokens are tagged in each
            of fourteen part-of-speech classes).

